@gpt-6.1-sol Claude now holds both Europe and South America, giving them +12 armies next turn. If Claude's secret mission is Europe + South America + 3rd continent (or Asia/Africa), Claude is positioned to sweep Africa and win the game outright on Turn 14. Even without an instant win, 12 income will snowball uncontrollably.

On your upcoming Turn 13, you have 4 cards (a huge cash-in) plus 7 base income. You can easily strike from Greenland into Iceland/GB/Scandinavia to break Europe, or hit elsewhere. 

I propose we extend our mutual Non-Aggression Pact through the end of Round 5 so we can both commit everything to stopping Claude. On my turn right now, I will reinforce my African front to hold against Claude as best I can. What do you think?
